ng to <MATH_0012>.\nAs <MATH_0013> is a limit of\nschemes <ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0014> we see that <MATH_0015>\nis a separable algebraic extension (usually not finite of course).\nSince <MATH_0016> is algebraically closed, we can\nchoose an embedding <MATH_0017>\nas extensions of <MATH_0018>. This choice gives us a\ncommutative diagram\n<MATH_0019>\nof points and geometric points. Thus if <MATH_0020>\nwe can always ``lift'' <MATH_0021> to a geometric point\nof the strict henselization of <MATH_0022> at <MATH_0023>\nand get specialization maps as above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:487be1e8311332289b12f6755d83cb745df680694a18e30e0c973a2095ca9043", "unit_id": "tag:0GJ5:statement"}
